    "body": "I've added the \"rest\" of this interface, as explained [here](https://github.com/mfreed7/declarative-shadow-dom/blob/master/README.md#serialization) in the explainer. In particular, the section just below that, [Closed shadow roots](https://github.com/mfreed7/declarative-shadow-dom/blob/master/README.md#closed-shadow-roots) goes into the details of the interface. You essentially get two knobs. `includeShadowRoots` is an opt-in for *any* shadow roots to be serialized. The second input, `closedRoots` is a list of closed shadow roots that you would like to be included. If a closed shadow root is encountered that is not in the list, it will be skipped to preserve encapsulation.\r\n\r\nI am going to add the corresponding change to my HTML spec PR.\r\n\r\nLMK if the above clarifies the situation, or if you have further questions.",
